{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the clear and righteous you shall not slay.</b> A wicked man who emerged clear and righteous in his trial, and afterward one who knew testimony against him came — from where do we learn that we do not bring him back? Scripture says: ״ונקי וצדיק אל תהרוג״ — 'and the clear and righteous you shall not slay' — ״כי לא אצדיק רשע״ — 'for I will not justify the wicked': if the court below justified him unwittingly, the Holy One, blessed be He, will not justify him in the court above."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:14.555020918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}